odex conversation back through\nthe provider that encrypted it, across accounts. The `encrypted_content`\nblocks embedded inside `agent_message` payloads were named as a scope cut in\nthat same release and never picked up, so inter-agent sessions stayed the one\nplace capture destroyed provider-withheld material rather than sealing it.\n\nNot a corner case: 126 of 165 `agent_message` response_items in the local\ncorpus carry encrypted blocks, and inter-agent traffic is exactly the sort of\nsession whose reasoning cannot be reconstructed from the visible turns.\n\nAn inter-agent message now becomes two events at the same seq — the visible\nturn, and a sealed `reasoning`-kind sibling whose raw.data is the line reduced\nto its encrypted blocks. The pairing, and the reason distinct kinds keep the\nids from colliding, are the same as a reasoning item with a populated summary.\nThe visible turn is unchanged: it still keeps a bare\n{type: \"encrypted_content\"} marker where a sealed block was, which is what\nmakes the split visible rather than silent.\n\nThe redaction stack already exempts `.../encrypted_content` on reasoning-kind\nevents, so pattern-matching cannot corrupt a blob it cannot read; the test\nasserts the stored blob byte-for-byte, which pins that exemption too.\n\nVerified against a real rollout: all 62 encrypted agent_message items\npreserved, blobs intact at 6-8KB each.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011yyjMrYMdcPPiKnPmUm8Hs\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/jobs/9a01c126/tmp/msg.txt","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"586aaef2-ad43-407f-89e5-655a42264a27","version":"2.1.222"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-05T02:25:35.992Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
